> Compare true and learned densities on the same grid and colour scale

All 16,384 grid centers lie in [-4,4]² at spacing 1/16. Rows run from high y
to low y in the saved source arrays. The plot explicitly reverses that storage
axis to draw physical y upward. Both panels use the same native terrain palette
and density range 0..0.20, with square cells and equal coordinate units. The
finite window is a visualization; it does not claim the density integrates to
one within this box. The exact global normalization follows the invertible map
and its Gaussian base, checked separately below.

