> Show the input-dependent volume factors on both paths

These panels retain each analytic determinant and its actual-Jacobian check.
Forward points use observed x0; inverse points use supplied Gaussian z0.
The other coordinate also affects the map, so a vertical spread at the same
horizontal coordinate is expected. These are point clouds, not single-variable
functions or paired forward/inverse observations.

